The Go rendering: an application whose iota groups are compared with constant
expressions of their types that are not member names: conversions of literals,
a declaration, max, a keyed literal and a return giving 2, a member of another
block, a constant of a block of its own, a constant a function body declares, a
constant whose type is spelled through an alias, a member converted to another
enumerated type inside a constant expression, the zero value, a member declared from another, and constants whose value differs by
target (the word size, a file constrained by a legacy build line only, files
named for an architecture).

